00:00:33.736 --> 00:00:35.405
- Vice-nah-vee?

00:00:35.405 --> 00:00:36.450
- Vish-nah-vee?

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:37.280
- Come on now.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.790
- Va-hash-uh-nee-vah.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:39.711
- Vaishnavi?

00:00:39.711 --> 00:00:42.336
- See, I'm so close at all
of these, I'm so close.

00:00:44.052 --> 00:00:46.585
- It looks like it's
pronounced as Anushka,

00:00:46.585 --> 00:00:47.709
but I bet you it's way off.

00:00:47.709 --> 00:00:48.550
- Anushka.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:49.387
- Anushka.

00:00:49.387 --> 00:00:50.714
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:50.714 --> 00:00:51.806
- I think I got that one.

00:00:53.482 --> 00:00:55.256
- Like a Vivian, like an Indian Vivian.

00:00:55.256 --> 00:00:55.889
- Viv-eck?

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.346
- Vivek, I know, 'cause
Vivek Shraya, the musician.

00:01:00.161 --> 00:01:01.767
- Vivek, oh, it's a guy's name. (laughs)

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:04.008
- Now, normally, it's
like too many letters,

00:01:04.008 --> 00:01:05.520
I'm not using them all,
but I feel like this one

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.240
could use a couple extra letters.

00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:10.105
- See, I wanna say it's Aayush,

00:01:10.105 --> 00:01:13.324
but I kinda think it's An-oosh.

00:01:13.324 --> 00:01:13.943
- Aayush?

00:01:13.943 --> 00:01:15.206
- Ai-you-shhh.

00:01:15.206 --> 00:01:17.255
- Too many A's, like Aaron.

00:01:19.154 --> 00:01:20.451
- Oh my god, what?

00:01:20.451 --> 00:01:22.476
- Choke, choke, Chokalingam?

00:01:22.476 --> 00:01:23.881
- Choke-uh-ling-gahm.

00:01:23.881 --> 00:01:25.206
- (laughs) That sounds dirty.

00:01:25.206 --> 00:01:28.102
- The way that I said it,
it sounded like a disease.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:30.588
- My-tea-lee?

00:01:30.588 --> 00:01:31.261
- Mutt-til-ee?

00:01:31.261 --> 00:01:32.385
- Okay, this one looks good.

00:01:32.385 --> 00:01:33.427
- We don't need that A there.

00:01:33.427 --> 00:01:37.515
- Mah, mah-eet-tuh-lee.

00:01:38.582 --> 00:01:39.511
Wait.

00:01:39.511 --> 00:01:40.362
- Got it.

00:01:41.669 --> 00:01:42.357
- Carrie.

00:01:42.357 --> 00:01:43.231
- Kah-ree?

00:01:43.231 --> 00:01:45.725
- Is it pronounced Car-eh, or just Car?

00:01:45.725 --> 00:01:47.716
- That's very sexy, Care-eh.

00:01:47.716 --> 00:01:49.822
- That sounds confident, right,
it's all about confidence

00:01:49.822 --> 00:01:51.482
in how you pronounce the
name, even if it's dead wrong.

00:01:51.482 --> 00:01:52.946
- I think the names are very beautiful.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:55.245
- Pronunciation of names
is really important,

00:01:55.245 --> 00:01:57.952
so even if it's super
hard, just try your hardest

00:01:57.952 --> 00:02:00.074
and don't automatically
go for the nickname

00:02:00.074 --> 00:02:02.133
because that's someone's
name, it's important.

